# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the Swift evaluation window (tp4/swift; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/swift and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-swift-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint with its own converted-weight directory (never the base's); a job without them is the base,
# byte for byte what production serves.
# L1 (TIMED, SWIFT of the first decode ABAB pair): the same profile and tests as C1, on Swift. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no
# build, no CI push, no other job beside it. CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: created|found" line, and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. READ:
# c2_smoke_check clean AND python3 scripts/ci/octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4 clean (the
# octo rounds ran on the new weights). Then, after the four boots of the pair (C1 L1 C2 L2): python3 scripts/ci/octo3_report.py --control-a <C1 smoke> --arm-a <L1 smoke>
# --control-b <C2 smoke> --arm-b <L2 smoke> --arm-container <L1 container> --arm-container <L2 container> --profile
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4: per test (concurrent8_steady, concurrent8_code_32k_long) the aggregate of the all-live window of Swift
# against the base's in BOTH pairs and the floors; here GAIN / PARITY / LOSS read Swift over base. The texts DIFFER by construction (another checkpoint: do not run
# octo_compare.py), and so do the lengths of the answers and the drafter's acceptance: the rate moves with tau (T1, T2), not with the engine, which is the same. TELEMETRY
# (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say
# decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the checkpoint. Duration (estimate): 40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k_long
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=70
